# Lord of Fate — a Two-color greater enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 7/12 Two-color greater enemies — 20 life, bribe 100 gold
# enemy: Lord of Fate (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0010.dck "Lord of Fate (Bl/Wh, 4th Edition)" [Tier 3
#   — Manalink 3 file dated 2016-02-15; its first 14 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 15
#   lines (60 cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/lord_of_fate.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 7)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/lord_of_fate.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Greater) — "Lord of Fate" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Lord of Fate
11 Plains
11 Swamp
2 Dark Ritual
3 Castle
3 Healing Salve
3 Holy Strength
3 Unholy Strength
4 Yotian Soldier
4 Serra Angel
3 Osai Vultures
3 Pestilence
2 Necropolis of Azar
3 Drudge Skeletons
2 Divine Transformation
3 Ornithopter
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Ornithopter
#   .vBlack  3 Brass Man
#   .vBlue   3 Ornithopter
#   .vGreen  3 Animate Dead
#   .vRed    3 Amulet of Kroog
#   .vWhite  3 Brass Man
SB: 3 Brass Man
SB: 3 Animate Dead
SB: 3 Amulet of Kroog
